                       v2.1 Written By: The Marshal


    Welcome to Bulletin Board System Statistics Generating Routine, v2.1.

    This program was written to be used on your BBS to give your users an
understanding of what makes your board tick. It will list such pieces of
information as how many users you have, how many are male and female, the
average age of the users, how many are long distance callers, or from out
of this country. It will also list how many users of each computer type you
have on your bbs, plus a whole screen more!!!

    Version 2.0 was written for two reasons. First, I wanted to make it run
both faster, and more smoothly. Secondly, the first version, as well as the
program from which I got this idea lacked one BIG criteria.

    One of the things this program does is to tell your users how many other
users on your BBS use the same computer as they do, and for those users that
are not using their computer, what computer ARE they using?

    The first two versions lacked the routines to adequately handle this
problem, unless the SysOp was using the nine(9) computer types originally
given to them upon C-Net's arrival.

    This version is capable of reading, and handling the possibility that a
SysOp has set up more, or less, than 9 different Computer Types, as given
in Menu # 30 of the BBSMENU file.  Up to 24 different computer types can
be configured to work with C-Net, and this program was written to handle
all of them, if need be.

    All computer types should be no more than 18 characters in length, or
this program will chop them TO this length. This shouldn't be too big a
problem as C-Net's longest default type is 16, so you shouldn't have any
problem sticking to this request.

    Version 2.1 was written to fix a problem that the newer versions of
C-Net incorporated, but that Ken never told anyone. He decided to change
the way he stored the GENDER information in the bbs.udata file. Because of
this change, BBS_Stats can not correctly count the number of male/female
users on your bbs. I've rewritten this version to correctly read Ken's new
way of storing the GENDER, but there's another problem. See the included
file "Gender_Checker" for more information...

    I tried very hard to keep all the statistical information on one 80
column formatted screen, but wasn't able to when the number of computer
types exceeded 15, so if you use 15 or fewer, this program will generate
everything it needs on one screen, but if you choose to go beyond 15, the
program will insert a "Press Any Key" type statement right before it will
display the Average Information.

    Both screen formats look very good, and are acceptable for use in both
your G-Files section, and inclusion in your "sys.welcome" file. Instructions
on how to do this can be found within the file itself, along with some
SysOp-Definable variables that you will want to set before you run this
file for the first time.

    A file called "BBS_Stats.Computers" will be created in your SysData
directory, and is NEW to this version of BBS_Stats. The program need only
create this file once, unless such a time comes when you choose to again
change the computer types, perhaps upon a new update or the like. If this
should ever happen, simply delete the file from your SysData directory,
and ReRun the BBS_Stats file.  It is written to check for it's existence
before either creating, or continuing...

